{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44129742",
      "title": "Interacting With The Underlying Form Object In The Component",
      "lectureOrder": 249,
      "videoOrder": 237,
      "sourceHash": "c1ed8b47f25c464c86a8885392dcea43dcc8aafb89eadf0bc10cc722038fbb2d",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.36,
          "end": 3.51,
          "en": "So at this point, we're almost done",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.51,
          "end": 5.43,
          "en": "with template driven forms",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.43,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "because you did learn about its key features now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.22,
          "end": 10.653,
          "en": "but there is a bit more we can do with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.7,
          "end": 14.37,
          "en": "For example, we might wanna reset the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.37,
          "end": 16.2,
          "en": "once it has been submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.2,
          "end": 17.85,
          "en": "And we could easily do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 21.6,
          "en": "by using this formData object we're getting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.6,
          "end": 24.33,
          "en": "and by accessing the form in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.33,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "And then here, we can call reset,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 30.45,
          "en": "and this will do just what the name implies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.45,
          "end": 34.86,
          "en": "It will clear the input values, and that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.86,
          "end": 39.33,
          "en": "It will also reset all the internally managed information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 39.33,
          "end": 40.89,
          "en": "about the form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.89,
          "end": 42.42,
          "en": "So whether it's valid or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.42,
          "end": 44.4,
          "en": "whether it has been touched or not,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.4,
          "end": 47.85,
          "en": "this will all be reset as you would expect,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.85,
          "end": 50.46,
          "en": "because of course if the form is submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.46,
          "end": 54.39,
          "en": "it should be treated as pristine and untouched again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.39,
          "end": 56.793,
          "en": "And that's also what reset will do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.93,
          "end": 60.12,
          "en": "In addition, it's also worth mentioning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 60.12,
          "end": 64.53,
          "en": "that you can see that there's a lot of other information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.53,
          "end": 65.7,
          "en": "in that form object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.7,
          "end": 68.78999999999999,
          "en": "and also some other interesting methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 68.78999999999999,
          "end": 70.563,
          "en": "you might wanna play around with.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 75.75,
          "en": "You could, for example, mark a form as dirty manually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.75,
          "end": 77.22,
          "en": "from inside your code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 77.22,
          "end": 81.03,
          "en": "if you had a use case where you need to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 81.03,
          "end": 83.03999999999999,
          "en": "Angular will manage it for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 83.03999999999999,
          "end": 85.95,
          "en": "But if you wanna overwrite Angular's behavior",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 85.95,
          "end": 88.17,
          "en": "at some point, you can do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 88.17,
          "end": 93.17,
          "en": "You can also add or remove validators programmatically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 93.21000000000001,
          "end": 95.52000000000001,
          "en": "if you need it to do that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 95.52000000000001,
          "end": 99.33,
          "en": "But these are of course also some more advanced use cases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.33,
          "end": 103.14,
          "en": "because typically, when using the template driven approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.14,
          "end": 106.44,
          "en": "you wanna do all the setup and configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 106.44,
          "end": 108.50999999999999,
          "en": "inside of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 108.50999999999999,
          "end": 112.41,
          "en": "That's the idea behind this approach after all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.41,
          "end": 115.773,
          "en": "And you'll learn about an alternative approach soon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.03,
          "end": 119.28,
          "en": "Nonetheless, it is worth knowing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.28,
          "end": 121.95,
          "en": "about these properties and methods here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 121.95,
          "end": 123.42,
          "en": "and I can only encourage you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.42,
          "end": 124.743,
          "en": "to play around with them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 125.85,
          "end": 128.46,
          "en": "Here, it's now reset, which I want to call.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 128.46,
          "end": 131.31,
          "en": "And with that being called here, if I save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 131.31,
          "end": 135.12,
          "en": "if I enter some valid values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.12,
          "end": 136.8,
          "en": "and I click Login,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.8,
          "end": 138.96,
          "en": "you see the inputs are cleared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 138.96,
          "end": 142.17000000000002,
          "en": "and you see that, for example, now this is treated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.17000000000002,
          "end": 144.453,
          "en": "as pristine and untouched again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 145.38,
          "end": 147.45,
          "en": "As you can tell by these classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.45,
          "end": 148.65,
          "en": "because as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.65,
          "end": 152.913,
          "en": "that is what Angular will do if you reset a form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.47,
          "end": 158.57999999999998,
          "en": "Now, to conclude this template-driven approach here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.57999999999998,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "I wanna enhance this login component by adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 164.25,
          "en": "a little bit of a more advanced feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.25,
          "end": 168.27,
          "en": "to this component and this form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 168.27,
          "end": 169.82999999999998,
          "en": "Because I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.82999999999998,
          "end": 173.73,
          "en": "that if a user visits this page and this form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.73,
          "end": 176.46,
          "en": "if they enter a value here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.46,
          "end": 180.66,
          "en": "and they then reload the page for whatever reason,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.66,
          "end": 184.2,
          "en": "I save that value that they entered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.2,
          "end": 186.6,
          "en": "and I repopulate,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 186.6,
          "end": 191.133,
          "en": "or I pre-populate that form with that saved value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.39,
          "end": 195.66,
          "en": "And that therefore in the end means that as a first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 195.66,
          "end": 198.81,
          "en": "we must save that value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.81,
          "end": 201.063,
          "en": "whilst the user is entering it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 202.05,
          "end": 203.82,
          "en": "And then if that page loads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.82,
          "end": 206.34,
          "en": "and if that component here loads,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.34,
          "end": 209.61,
          "en": "I want to pre-populate this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.61,
          "end": 212.19299999999998,
          "en": "with the saved value if I have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.99,
          "end": 218.22,
          "en": "Now, let's start with saving that value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.22,
          "end": 222.3,
          "en": "To do that, I need access to this form outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 222.3,
          "end": 225.36,
          "en": "of on submit because I wanna start saving",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.36,
          "end": 229.07999999999998,
          "en": "right from the start when this component becomes active,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.07999999999998,
          "end": 231.39,
          "en": "not just when the form is submitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 231.39,
          "end": 234.213,
          "en": "There it's too late for what I want to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 235.74,
          "end": 239.61,
          "en": "So therefore here I'll add a new property called form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.61,
          "end": 243.6,
          "en": "and I'll use the viewChild function to populate it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.6,
          "end": 245.4,
          "en": "And you of course learned about this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.4,
          "end": 246.54,
          "en": "before in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.54,
          "end": 250.32,
          "en": "We can use it to get hold of that form object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 250.32,
          "end": 251.313,
          "en": "in our template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.33,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "So I'm using form here as a selector to select this variable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 258.39,
          "en": "and the object stored in there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 258.39,
          "end": 261.24,
          "en": "and get access to it in my template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 261.24,
          "end": 265.44,
          "en": "So form here is now that form that is created by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 265.44,
          "end": 268.14,
          "en": "this formData object here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.14,
          "end": 270.96,
          "en": "And therefore viewChild will, in the end, give me an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 270.96,
          "end": 272.64300000000003,
          "en": "of type NgForm here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.35,
          "end": 278.85,
          "en": "This then allows me to add the constructor",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.85,
          "end": 282.65999999999997,
          "en": "and use afterNextRender,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 282.65999999999997,
          "end": 285.09000000000003,
          "en": "a function about which you also learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 285.09000000000003,
          "end": 286.71,
          "en": "earlier in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 286.71,
          "end": 290.46,
          "en": "to register a function that should be executed once,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 290.46,
          "end": 294.003,
          "en": "once this component has been rendered for the first time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 295.44,
          "end": 297.65999999999997,
          "en": "And I'm using afterNextRender",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 297.65999999999997,
          "end": 299.82,
          "en": "because this form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 299.82,
          "end": 302.37,
          "en": "since we're using the template-driven approach,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 302.37,
          "end": 305.22,
          "en": "is created with help of the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 305.22,
          "end": 308.82,
          "en": "So it's only after the template rendering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 308.82,
          "end": 312.333,
          "en": "that this form is fully initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 313.44,
          "end": 316.74,
          "en": "That's why I'm using this afterNextRender hook here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 316.74,
          "end": 318.963,
          "en": "to interact with that form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 319.98,
          "end": 322.92,
          "en": "So inside of this afterNextRender function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 322.92,
          "end": 326.46,
          "en": "I can then get hold of that form and read it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 326.46,
          "end": 330.21,
          "en": "Since I'm using the viewChild function, this is a Signal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 330.21,
          "end": 332.90999999999997,
          "en": "so I need to read it like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 332.90999999999997,
          "end": 336.42,
          "en": "And then there, I wanna be notified",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 336.42,
          "end": 339.78,
          "en": "about any changes the user makes to the form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 339.78,
          "end": 343.11,
          "en": "so that I can save that information",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 343.11,
          "end": 345.063,
          "en": "somewhere in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 346.23,
          "end": 349.23,
          "en": "Now it turns out that Angular gives you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 349.23,
          "end": 354.23,
          "en": "a valueChanges property on that form object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 354.42,
          "end": 357.72,
          "en": "and that then gives you an Observable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 357.72,
          "end": 360.3,
          "en": "a feature about which you learned before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 360.3,
          "end": 363.66,
          "en": "and a feature which I mentioned would be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 363.66,
          "end": 368.01,
          "en": "from time to time in certain parts of Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 368.01,
          "end": 371.1,
          "en": "Well, valueChanges now is such a part",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 371.1,
          "end": 373.44,
          "en": "that does use an Observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 373.44,
          "end": 375.33,
          "en": "And we need that question mark here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 375.33,
          "end": 377.61,
          "en": "since TypeScript is not convinced",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 377.61,
          "end": 381.3,
          "en": "that form will yield a value here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 381.3,
          "end": 382.23,
          "en": "We could change this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 382.23,
          "end": 385.65,
          "en": "by changing this to be a required viewChild.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 385.65,
          "end": 388.263,
          "en": "With that, we can get rid of the question mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 389.7,
          "end": 392.82,
          "en": "So now, valueChanges gives us an Observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 392.82,
          "end": 397.62,
          "en": "And we can subscribe to that to be notified about changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 397.62,
          "end": 401.97,
          "en": "because this is an Observable set up by Angular",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 401.97,
          "end": 404.61,
          "en": "that will emit new values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 404.61,
          "end": 409.44,
          "en": "whenever the values entered into the form change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 409.44,
          "end": 413.073,
          "en": "So essentially, on every keystroke the user makes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 414,
          "end": 416.43,
          "en": "Now, here a question mark is needed as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 416.43,
          "end": 420.36,
          "en": "because again, this could be undefined, it could be null,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 420.36,
          "end": 422.25,
          "en": "and therefore we need a question mark.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 422.25,
          "end": 426.93,
          "en": "So that subscription is only set up if valueChanges exists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 426.93,
          "end": 429.6,
          "en": "so if this Observable exists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 429.6,
          "end": 431.04,
          "en": "because it might not exist",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 431.04,
          "end": 433.923,
          "en": "if the form hasn't been fully initialized yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 435.36,
          "end": 437.64,
          "en": "So we can set up this subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 437.64,
          "end": 440.97,
          "en": "and we can pass our observer object to it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 440.97,
          "end": 444.51,
          "en": "and then register this next function that will be executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 444.51,
          "end": 447.36,
          "en": "for every new value that is omitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 447.36,
          "end": 450.36,
          "en": "And I shared more details about Observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 450.36,
          "end": 452.01,
          "en": "and this next function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 452.01,
          "end": 455.82,
          "en": "in that earlier RxJS course section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 455.82,
          "end": 457.65,
          "en": "So definitely take a look at that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 457.65,
          "end": 459.753,
          "en": "if this is all brand new to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 460.77,
          "end": 463.77,
          "en": "Now here, we'll get that value that is omitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 463.77,
          "end": 465.96,
          "en": "which here is of type any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 465.96,
          "end": 467.25,
          "en": "And therefore here for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 467.25,
          "end": 468.993,
          "en": "I'll simply console.log it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 470.37,
          "end": 473.28,
          "en": "And of course, since I call subscribe here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 473.28,
          "end": 476.19,
          "en": "I'll get back a subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 476.19,
          "end": 479.07,
          "en": "and I want to clean up that subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 479.07,
          "end": 482.61,
          "en": "whenever this login component gets destroyed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 482.61,
          "end": 484.65,
          "en": "because even though we never destroy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 484.65,
          "end": 486.33,
          "en": "this component anywhere,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 486.33,
          "end": 488.25,
          "en": "it could theoretically be removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 488.25,
          "end": 491.76,
          "en": "if we change our application and to then make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 491.76,
          "end": 494.34,
          "en": "that we don't have some ongoing subscription,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 494.34,
          "end": 496.05,
          "en": "which we don't need anymore.",
