        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 496.05,
          "end": 500.943,
          "en": "We should always clean up our RxJS subscriptions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 501.87,
          "end": 504.25,
          "en": "So here, I'll get my destroyRef",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 505.26,
          "end": 507.267,
          "en": "with help of inject(DestroyRef).",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 510.09,
          "end": 513.45,
          "en": "And then here in afterNextRender,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 513.45,
          "end": 518.373,
          "en": "I will use this.destroyRef.onDestroy",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 519.6,
          "end": 523.68,
          "en": "and call subscription?.unsubscribe like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 523.68,
          "end": 525.573,
          "en": "if the subscription exists.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 526.62,
          "end": 529.74,
          "en": "That's why this question mark here is needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 529.74,
          "end": 532.92,
          "en": "Okay, so with that in place, if we now save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 532.92,
          "end": 534.84,
          "en": "you'll see I get some output initially here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 534.84,
          "end": 536.94,
          "en": "when the form is initialized.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 536.94,
          "end": 538.71,
          "en": "And now if I start typing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 538.71,
          "end": 542.97,
          "en": "you see with every keystroke I get an updated object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 542.97,
          "end": 544.71,
          "en": "And that's also interesting.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 544.71,
          "end": 549.71,
          "en": "You see that the value we get here in our next function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 549.9,
          "end": 552.57,
          "en": "is, in the end, an object of this shape,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 552.57,
          "end": 556.773,
          "en": "an object with an email property and a password property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 557.64,
          "end": 560.7,
          "en": "Now, in this case here, I only wanna save the email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 560.7,
          "end": 565.7,
          "en": "because saving passwords doesn't sound like a secure idea.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 566.37,
          "end": 568.5,
          "en": "And hence, if I want to do that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 568.5,
          "end": 571.383,
          "en": "I need to access value.email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 572.7,
          "end": 577.533,
          "en": "And I now want save that in the local storage of my browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 579.48,
          "end": 582.33,
          "en": "So here, in this next function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 582.33,
          "end": 585.51,
          "en": "I want to access window.localStorage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 585.51,
          "end": 590.13,
          "en": "to use the browser built in local storage feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 590.13,
          "end": 593.46,
          "en": "which is some storage provided by all browsers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 593.46,
          "end": 595.23,
          "en": "And we can call set.Item here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 595.23,
          "end": 597.633,
          "en": "to save something in that storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 598.89,
          "end": 601.71,
          "en": "Now, we need to give that an identifier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 601.71,
          "end": 604.92,
          "en": "and I'll name it saved-login-form,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 604.92,
          "end": 608.25,
          "en": "and then a value that should be saved.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 608.25,
          "end": 613.05,
          "en": "And here, in my case, I want to save that email address,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 613.05,
          "end": 616.54,
          "en": "but I'll actually save it as an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 617.55,
          "end": 621.3,
          "en": "where email is set to value.email.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 621.3,
          "end": 625.35,
          "en": "But since local storage only accepts string values,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 625.35,
          "end": 629.79,
          "en": "I will call JSON.stringify to convert this object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 629.79,
          "end": 632.643,
          "en": "to a string in the JSON format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 633.6,
          "end": 636,
          "en": "And with that, this object should be stored",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 636,
          "end": 638.58,
          "en": "in the local storage with every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 638.58,
          "end": 640.65,
          "en": "and therefore it should also be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 640.65,
          "end": 642.273,
          "en": "with every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 643.92,
          "end": 647.04,
          "en": "So if we now check the Application tab",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 647.04,
          "end": 650.52,
          "en": "in the browser developer tools, because it's there",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 650.52,
          "end": 654.99,
          "en": "where you can access information about your local storage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 654.99,
          "end": 657.87,
          "en": "You should see the saved-login-form key here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 657.87,
          "end": 659.433,
          "en": "with that empty form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 660.36,
          "end": 661.77,
          "en": "But if I now enter something here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 661.77,
          "end": 665.58,
          "en": "you see it updates with every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 665.58,
          "end": 667.05,
          "en": "So that works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 212,
          "start": 667.05,
          "end": 670.62,
          "en": "And knowing about this valueChanges Observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 213,
          "start": 670.62,
          "end": 673.14,
          "en": "is definitely useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 214,
          "start": 673.14,
          "end": 674.97,
          "en": "However, of course at the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 215,
          "start": 674.97,
          "end": 679.17,
          "en": "we're basically updating local storage on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 216,
          "start": 679.17,
          "end": 681.51,
          "en": "And whilst this is not a problem here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 217,
          "start": 681.51,
          "end": 685.95,
          "en": "in this basic application, it is probably easy to imagine",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 218,
          "start": 685.95,
          "end": 689.16,
          "en": "that this might not be ideal for performance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 219,
          "start": 689.16,
          "end": 692.823,
          "en": "if this were a more complex application or form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 220,
          "start": 693.66,
          "end": 698.64,
          "en": "Therefore, here, I'll actually call pipe before subscribing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 221,
          "start": 698.64,
          "end": 703.64,
          "en": "because RxJS, as you learned, offers tons of operators,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 222,
          "start": 704.22,
          "end": 706.11,
          "en": "which can be overwhelming,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 223,
          "start": 706.11,
          "end": 710.373,
          "en": "but if, for example, offers a debounceTime operator,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 224,
          "start": 712.14,
          "end": 715.383,
          "en": "and this must be imported from RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 225,
          "start": 716.94,
          "end": 720.75,
          "en": "And what debounceTime will do is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 226,
          "start": 720.75,
          "end": 724.443,
          "en": "it takes a time in milliseconds, let's say 500,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 227,
          "start": 725.46,
          "end": 729.48,
          "en": "and if a new value is emitted within that timeframe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 228,
          "start": 729.48,
          "end": 732.06,
          "en": "after the previous value has been omitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 229,
          "start": 732.06,
          "end": 735.48,
          "en": "then it will discard that latest value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 230,
          "start": 735.48,
          "end": 737.25,
          "en": "So it will essentially make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 231,
          "start": 737.25,
          "end": 740.1,
          "en": "that this next function doesn't get triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 232,
          "start": 740.1,
          "end": 742.53,
          "en": "if the user is still typing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 233,
          "start": 742.53,
          "end": 746.37,
          "en": "Only if the user stops for at least 500 seconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 234,
          "start": 746.37,
          "end": 750.81,
          "en": "the emitted value will make it to this next function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 235,
          "start": 750.81,
          "end": 751.92,
          "en": "So that will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 236,
          "start": 751.92,
          "end": 754.713,
          "en": "that this next function won't run too often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 237,
          "start": 756.15,
          "end": 759.72,
          "en": "With that, if we save this, if I reload, you see, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 238,
          "start": 759.72,
          "end": 761.82,
          "en": "I start with this empty field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 239,
          "start": 761.82,
          "end": 764.43,
          "en": "but now if I type here, it does not update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 240,
          "start": 764.43,
          "end": 766.38,
          "en": "as long as I keep on typing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 241,
          "start": 766.38,
          "end": 770.61,
          "en": "Only if I then stop typing for at least 500 milliseconds,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 242,
          "start": 770.61,
          "end": 774.45,
          "en": "this gets updated, and that's therefore more efficient",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 243,
          "start": 774.45,
          "end": 777.21,
          "en": "in how we can leverage the fact that we're dealing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 244,
          "start": 777.21,
          "end": 779.37,
          "en": "with an Observable here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 245,
          "start": 779.37,
          "end": 781.17,
          "en": "But with that, let's now make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 246,
          "start": 781.17,
          "end": 783.21,
          "en": "that we don't just save that value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 247,
          "start": 783.21,
          "end": 786.42,
          "en": "but that we instead also use a saved value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 248,
          "start": 786.42,
          "end": 788.643,
          "en": "to pre-populate the form.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
